  "title": "Namaz of the Bedouin (Salat al-A'rabi)",
  "data": "When the daylight rises, offer a two-unit prayer. In the first unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Falaq](A117) seven times; in the second, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Nas](A118) seven times. After the taslim, recite [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) seven times.\nThen offer eight units of prayer with two taslims: sit after every two units without saying the taslim, and say the taslim after the fourth unit; then offer the other four units in the same way. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once, [Surah al-Nasr](A114) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) twenty-five times.\nAfter the tashahhud and taslim, repeat the following supplication seven times:\nيَا حَيُّ يَا قَيُّوْمُ يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA HAYYU YAA QAYYOOMU YAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nO Ever-living! O Self-subsisting! O Lord of Majesty and Honor!\nيَا اِلٰهَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nYAA ILAAHAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN\nO God of the first and the last!\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Most Merciful of all who show mercy!\nيَا رَحْمٰنَ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَرَحِيْمَهُمَا\nYAA RAHMAANAD DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRATI WA RAHEEMAHUMAA\nO Beneficent of this world and the Hereafter, and Merciful in both!\nيَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ\nYAA RABBI YAA RABBI YAA RABBI YAA RABBI YAA RABBI YAA RABBI YAA RABB\nO my Lord! (seven times)\nيَا اَللّٰهُ يَا اَللّٰهُ يَا اَللّٰهُ يَا اَللّٰهُ يَا اَللّٰهُ يَا اَللّٰهُ يَا اَللّٰهُ\nYAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAH\nO Allah! (seven times)\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهٖ وَاغْفِرْ لِيْ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WAGHFIR LEE\nSend blessings upon Muhammad and his Household, and forgive me.\nYou may now mention what you need. Then repeat the following seventy times:\nلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ سُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيْمِ\nLAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEMI SUBHAANALLAAHI RABBIL A'RSHIL KAREEM\nThere is no might and no strength save in Allah, the High, the Great. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Honored Throne.\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيْمِ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI RABBIL A'RSHIL KAREEM\nGlory be to Allah, Lord of the Honored Throne.\nIn his book of Misbah al-Mutahajjid, Shaykh al-Tusi has described this prayer without the supplication above; instead, he says that when you finish the prayer, repeat the following seventy times:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيْمِ وَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI RABBIL A'RSHIL KAREEMI WA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nGlory be to Allah, Lord of the Honored Throne. There is no might and no strength save in Allah, the High, the Great.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has reported the following from Shaykh al-Tal'akbari through his own chain of authority connected to Zayd ibn Thabit:\nOne day, a man from the Bedouins stood up before the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and said, \"May Allah accept my father and mother as ransoms for you, O Allah's Messenger. We live in the desert away from al-Madinah and it is not feasible for us to present ourselves every Friday before you. I therefore want you to teach me an act which collects the rewards of performing the Friday Prayer, so that when I return to my people I will teach it to them.\"\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) taught him this prayer, and then said: \"I swear by Him Who has sent me and chosen me in truth, I will certainly guarantee Paradise for any believer, man or woman, who offers this prayer exactly as I have explained. Moreover, he who offers this prayer will not leave his place before Almighty Allah has forgiven his and his parents' sins, given him the reward of every individual who performed a prayer in all regions of the Muslims, recorded for him the reward of every individual in the east and the west of the earth who observed fasting and offered prayers on that day, and given him rewards that no eye has ever seen and no ear has ever heard.\""
}
